[[File:Brutal black dragon icon.png|left]]
'''Brutal black dragons''' are [[slayer monsters]] found in the [[Catacombs of Kourend]]. Requiring level 77 [[Slayer]] in order to be damaged, they are a tougher but more rewarding version of [[black dragon]]s and as such can be killed as an alternative for a black dragon [[Slayer task]].

Players can access the dragons by running west through the Catacombs of Kourend, past the [[Brutal blue dragon|brutal blue]] and [[Brutal red dragon|brutal red dragons]]. Alternatively, use the {{Map|type=maplink|text=hole|mtype=circle|r=4|1563,3791}} found in [[Lovakengj]], reached by using the "Jewellery of Jubilation" teleport option on the [[Book of the Dead]] and running north-east, or the "Xeric's Inferno" teleport option on a [[Xeric's talisman]] and running east. (unlocking this shortcut requires climbing up the vine from inside the catacombs first).

Like all [[brutal dragon]]s, they use [[Melee]], [[Magic]] and long-range [[dragonfire]]. Using both [[Protect from Magic]] and an [[antifire potion]] will completely protect players from their dragonfire and magic attacks, and they can be safespotted this way if not standing within melee range.

Brutal black dragons are the only monster to have a [[dragon spear]] drop not on the [[rare drop table]]. Nevertheless, for players seeking to obtain the spear as a drop, killing [[Gorak|goraks]] while wearing a [[ring of wealth]] is a better alternative.

